     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-10-24 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Actor Zaheer Iqbal reflects on career growth and film selection</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Zaheer Iqbal, who debuted in 2019, has shifted his focus from the glamour of acting to the craft itself. He stated that he now prioritizes good scripts and diverse characters over high-speed shots and traditional hero roles, emphasizing that every film contributes to his professional development. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/actor-zaheer-iqbal-reflects-on-career-growth-and-film-select.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Currently starring in the psychological thriller Tu Hai Meri Kiran, Iqbal noted that he seeks roles that challenge him. He also reflected on his 2024 marriage to Sonakshi Sinha, asserting that thorough mutual understanding before marriage is essential for a successful relationship.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate and concise summary of the actor's shift in focus and his personal views on marriage.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
