     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-24 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by NDTV Sports, BBC Sport">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>Bayern Munich Manager Vincent Kompany Collapses After Training, Hospitalised</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Football</span> <span>#Sports</span> <span>#Bayern Munich</span> <span>#Vincent Kompany</span></div>
       <p>Bayern Munich manager Vincent Kompany collapsed after a training session in Munich on Friday and was immediately taken to hospital by ambulance, according to NDTV Sports. The club confirmed he would remain under medical care for further examinations. BBC Sport further specified that Kompany collapsed while watching the club's second team train.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/bayern-munich-manager-vincent-kompany-collapses-after-traini.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In a statement, Bayern confirmed, &quot;Vincent Kompany had to seek medical treatment on Friday after collapsing during training for FC Bayern's amateurs.&quot; The club added that Kompany would undergo a thorough examination and remain under medical care, with his coaching staff managing training and match operations for the time being.</p><p>The incident follows Kompany's complaints of pain in his leg and hip, which he experienced days earlier ahead of Bayern's UEFA Champions League match against Arsenal on Wednesday. This discomfort was believed to be linked to a virus he had been suffering from, as reported by NDTV Sports. Bayern assistant coach Aaron Danks addressed the media in Kompany's absence, explaining that the manager required time to recover. Danks stated, &quot;It's just a virus. The doctors, the experts, know way more than I do.&quot; He emphasized the importance of rest, adding, &quot;The most important thing is that he rests and takes the time he needs, whatever that may be and however long that may be.&quot;</p><p>Despite his illness, Kompany had been on the bench for Bayern's match against RB Leipzig on Saturday, though he appeared subdued and remained seated throughout the game. Sporting director Max Eberl also indicated Kompany's physical struggles, noting he needed assistance to climb stairs due to the virus. While Kompany's coaching staff will oversee operations, no additional details about his condition or the expected duration of his absence have been announced by the club.</p><p>What to watch: Further updates on Kompany's health and return to duties.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is well-sourced, incorporates all provided details, and correctly attributes information to the respective outlets.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>How this was reported · 2 sources</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/football/bayern-munich-manager-vincent-kompany-collapses-after-training-session-taken-to-hospital-12227469#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li><li><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/ck3r5792en7go?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" rel="noopener">BBC Sport</a></li></ul>
      <p>Synthesised from 2 independent reports on the same event. Details are attributed to the outlet that carried them; nothing outside these sources is published.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-24/bayern-munich-manager-vincent-kompany-collapses-after-traini" data-title="Bayern Munich Manager Vincent Kompany Collapses After Training, Hospitalised"><b>Share:</b>
