     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-24 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>BJP Leader Proposes Three-Point Plan to Mitigate El Niño Impact in Telangana</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Senior BJP leader Gudur Narayana Reddy has proposed a three-point action plan to address water, agricultural, and power challenges in Telangana caused by El Niño. His strategy includes forming a time-bound technical cell of irrigation experts and agronomists to coordinate drought-mitigation measures.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/bjp-leader-proposes-three-point-plan-to-mitigate-el-nino-imp.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Reddy also urged the state to prioritize community-level groundwater recharge, such as desilting tanks and creating farm ponds, before peak summer. Finally, he recommended launching a public monitoring dashboard to track reservoir releases, drinking water tanker movements, and electricity supply hours for agricultural feeders.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately outlines the three-point plan proposed by the BJP leader to address El Niño impacts.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/telangana/bjp-leader-suggests-technical-cell-water-dashboard-to-tackle-el-nino-impact/article71620021.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
