     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-24 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>'Boys Becoming Men': Gautam Gambhir Lauds India's Youngsters After Gutsy T20I Win</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#T20I</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#New Zealand</span></div>
       <p>India secured a remarkable four-wicket victory over New Zealand in the 2nd T20I at Hagley Oval, Christchurch, on Saturday, October 24, 2026. Chasing a target of 181, the visitors found themselves in trouble at 70 for 5 in the 11th over after a steady start of 40 for 0. However, three young batters combined to take India over the line with one ball to spare, sealing a 2-0 series lead.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/boys-becoming-men-gautam-gambhir-lauds-indias-youngsters-aft.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Following the match, India head coach Gautam Gambhir lauded the team's youngsters, posting photographs of Tilak Varma, Naman Dhir, and Nitish Kumar Reddy on his X account. His caption, &quot;Boys becoming Men,&quot; paid tribute to the performances that turned the chase around when the innings appeared to be slipping away.</p><p>Naman Dhir, 26, contributed a crucial 31 runs off just 17 balls, including one four and three sixes, after walking in during the crisis. His knock in the 15th over provided the necessary momentum. Nitish Kumar Reddy, who turned 23 in May, then arrived at the crease after Dhir's dismissal and finished on 26 off 13 balls. Reddy's contribution alongside vice-captain Tilak Varma proved decisive as India reached 181 for 6 in 19.5 overs.</p><p>Tilak Varma, 23, was named Player of the Match for his unbeaten 51 off 26 balls, also taking two catches in the field. His innings anchored the final push after the top order collapse. For New Zealand, Mitchell Santner was the pick of the bowlers, taking 4 wickets for 21 runs. With the bat, Glenn Phillips top-scored with 70, and Jacobs added 58, helping New Zealand post 180 for 5 in their 20 overs. Arshdeep Singh was India's most successful bowler, securing 2 wickets for 33 runs.</p><p>This victory puts India 2-0 ahead in the series and continues a positive run for the three-time T20 World Cup winners, demonstrating their young players' ability to deliver under pressure in a high-scoring chase away from home.</p><p>What to watch: The performance of India's young talent in upcoming matches.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively summarizes the match details, player performances, and the coach's reaction, utilizing all provided facts.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/social-tracker-cricket/boys-becoming-men-gautam-gambhir-lauds-indias-youngsters-after-gutsy-2nd-t20i-win-vs-new-zealand/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
