  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/defence">defence</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="defence">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-10-24 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Centre Plans 60,000-Volunteer Civil Defence Network with Army Training Across 12 States</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#Civil Defence</span> <span>#Indian Army</span> <span>#Volunteers</span></div>
       <p>The Centre is planning to establish a comprehensive civil defence network comprising 60,000 volunteers across 12 states and Union Territories (UTs), with the Indian Army slated to provide the necessary training. This initiative aims to bolster the nation's civil defence capabilities by creating a robust volunteer network, as reported by Telegraph India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/centre-plans-60000-volunteer-civil-defence-network-with-army.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>According to News On AIR, the Indian Army's role will specifically involve training Civil Defence Master Trainers. Further details from Defence.in clarify that the Indian Army is set to train 600 Civil Defence master trainers. These trainers will then be instrumental in building the broader volunteer network across the designated 12 states and UTs.</p><p>The strategic involvement of the Indian Army underscores the importance placed on professional and structured training for this extensive civil defence force. The program's focus on master trainers suggests a cascaded training model, ensuring expertise is disseminated effectively throughout the volunteer base to enhance preparedness and response capabilities for various emergencies.</p><p>What to watch: The rollout schedule and selection process for the master trainers and volunteers.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively consolidates information from multiple sources to provide a clear and accurate summary of the training initiative.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en" rel="noopener">Defence (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-24/centre-plans-60000-volunteer-civil-defence-network-with-army" data-title="Centre Plans 60,000-Volunteer Civil Defence Network with Army Training Across 12 States"><b>Share:</b>
         <a class="sh-wa" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 1.8A6.2 6.2 0 0 0 2.7 11L1.8 14.2l3.3-.9A6.2 6.2 0 1 0 8 1.8z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>WhatsApp</a> ·
