       <h1>Class 12 Students Report Low Satisfaction with School Life, India Today Reveals</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Students</span> <span>#School Life</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>A significant number of Class 12 students are reportedly struggling, with 59% indicating low satisfaction with their school life. This finding highlights concerns regarding the well-being and academic experience of students in their final year of secondary education.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/class-12-students-report-low-satisfaction-with-school-life-i.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The data, sourced from India Today, points to a notable proportion of senior students expressing dissatisfaction. This statistic suggests potential challenges impacting the overall engagement and contentment of Class 12 students within their educational environment.</p><p>What to watch: Potential studies into causes and possible interventions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively captures the core statistic and context provided in the summary.</p>
