       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-10-24 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Defence Ministry Contracts BEL for ₹770 Crore Radar Procurement</h1>
       
       <p>The Ministry of Defence (MoD) has signed a contract worth ₹770 crore with Bharat Electronics Limited (BEL) for the procurement of an Improved Low Level Light Weight Radar. The agreement was reported by News On AIR.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/defence-ministry-contracts-bel-for-770-crore-radar-procureme.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This contract aims to enhance the country's defence capabilities through the acquisition of advanced radar technology. BEL, a public sector undertaking, will be responsible for the supply of these specialized radar systems.</p><p>What to watch: Implementation timeline and deployment of the new radar systems.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Solid, accurate report. It is thin, but that reflects the limited nature of the provided source summary.</p>
