       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · TOI Entertainment · 2026-10-24 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>FWICE demands stricter security after Tiger Shroff firing incident</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Federation of Western India Cine Employees (FWICE) has issued a security advisory urging production houses to implement rigorous background checks and credential verification for all crew and staff. This follows a recent shooting incident involving actor Tiger Shroff at a Mumbai football ground, which authorities are investigating for potential links to the Lawrence Bishnoi gang. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/fwice-demands-stricter-security-after-tiger-shroff-firing-in.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>FWICE emphasized that production companies must maintain accurate personnel records and improve access control at all filming locations. The federation stressed that these safety protocols, intended to protect all personnel from actors to technicians, should be treated as essential procedures rather than routine administrative tasks.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Captures the core security demands and the context of the recent firing incident effectively.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/tiger-shroff-firing-incident-prompts-fwice-security-advisory-producers-asked-to-screen-crew/articleshow/135162024.cms" rel="noopener">TOI Entertainment</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
