     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-24 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India and Uzbekistan review bilateral ties in Baku meeting</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>External Affairs Minister S. Jaishankar met with his Uzbek counterpart, Bakhtiyor Saidov, in Baku on Friday to discuss key bilateral issues. The ministers emphasized the urgent need to implement agreements reached at the highest level, building on a year of frequent high-level exchanges between the two nations.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/india-and-uzbekistan-review-bilateral-ties-in-baku-meeting.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This meeting follows Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s August visit to Uzbekistan, where he received the nation’s highest foreign honour, the Oliy Darajali Do'stlik Order. During that visit, India and Uzbekistan upgraded their relationship to a comprehensive strategic partnership, establishing a $5 billion bilateral trade target and signing 11 cooperation agreements.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively synthesizes the bilateral meeting details and relevant background information provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
