     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-24 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>INDIA Bloc Plans 'Public Impeachment' of Election Commissioner</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The INDIA bloc has announced a 'public impeachment proceeding' against Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar, scheduled for October 30, 2026. Congress leader K.C. Venugopal confirmed the move, noting that party leaders are being mobilized to participate in Delhi to protest against alleged electoral irregularities.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/india-bloc-plans-public-impeachment-of-election-commissioner.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Following the impeachment event, the coalition plans a 'Dilli Chalo March' on November 1st, culminating at Ramleela Maidan. Organizers expect at least one million citizens to join the demonstration against what they term 'Vote Chori' (vote theft). Congress president Mallikarjun Kharge has requested full participation from all alliance partners.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise reporting of the planned political protest and the specific terminology used by the INDIA bloc.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/india-bloc-public-impeachment-cec-gyanesh-kumar-amid-protest/article71621030.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
