     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-10-24 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>ITAT Ruling: Adjoining Flats May Qualify as Single Residential House for Tax Exemption</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#finance</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Mumbai bench of the Income Tax Appellate Tribunal (ITAT) has ruled that two adjoining flats can be treated as a single residential unit for Section 54F capital gains tax exemptions. The exemption is not automatically granted by purchase but requires physical verification to confirm the units are interconnected and used as one home. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/itat-ruling-adjoining-flats-may-qualify-as-single-residentia.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Legal obstacles such as separate registration deeds, individual flat numbers, or lack of formal amalgamation approval do not inherently disqualify claims. Assessing officers must instead evaluate evidence of a shared layout, common access, and unified residential use to determine eligibility.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief concisely captures the core legal ruling and the specific conditions required for the tax exemption.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/personal-finance/buying-two-flats-and-joining-them-itat-ruling-clarifies-when-you-can-claim-capital-gains-tax-exemption-11792849808703.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-24/itat-ruling-adjoining-flats-may-qualify-as-single-residentia" data-title="ITAT Ruling: Adjoining Flats May Qualify as Single Residential House for Tax Exemption"><b>Share:</b>
         <a class="sh-wa" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 1.8A6.2 6.2 0 0 0 2.7 11L1.8 14.2l3.3-.9A6.2 6.2 0 1 0 8 1.8z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>WhatsApp</a> ·
         <a class="sh-tg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M14.4 1.6 1.6 7l3.6 1.2L6 13l2.2-3.1 3.4 2.4 2.8-10.7z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Telegram</a> ·
