       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-24 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Kargil Democratic Alliance Warns of Agitation Over MHA Policy</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Kargil Democratic Alliance (KDA) has accused the Union Ministry of Home Affairs (MHA) and the Ladakh administration of using fear and intimidation, likening their tactics to ancient pharaohs. Co-chairperson Asgar Ali Karbalai stated that if the MHA fails to adhere to the May 22 agenda, the KDA and Leh Apex Body will initiate street protests and seek arrest to defend their constitutional rights.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/kargil-democratic-alliance-warns-of-agitation-over-mha-polic.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Demands include statehood, inclusion in the Constitution's 6th Schedule, and separate Lok Sabha seats. The KDA specifically opposes the October 15 proposal to establish a North East Frontier Agency-style body, arguing it prioritizes bureaucracy over the proposed elected legislature.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively captures the KDA's grievances and warnings using the source's provided context and specific terminology.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/ladakh/mha-employing-tools-of-fear-intimidation-and-threats-in-ladakh-kargil-democratic-alliance/article71620954.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
