     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-24 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Kerala Governor's vegetarian kitchen directive sparks political controversy</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Newly appointed Kerala Governor Om Prakash Mathur has faced backlash from the Congress and CPI(M) after reportedly directing the Lok Bhavan kitchen to serve only vegetarian food. While governor's office sources clarified that the policy reflects Mathur's personal diet and applies only to him and select staff, critics argue it infringes on individual freedom. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/kerala-governors-vegetarian-kitchen-directive-sparks-politic.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Congress leader KC Venugopal alleged that the move violates constitutional rights and constitutes an attempt to impose a 'saffron agenda' on the state. Home Minister Ramesh Chennithala echoed these concerns, maintaining that dietary choices are matters of personal liberty that should not be dictated by authorities.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Correctly summarizes the controversy and clarifies the specific scope of the kitchen directive as stated in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/keralam-governors-vegetarian-only-kitchen-order-sparks-row-congress-cpim-allege-saffron-agenda-ws-l-10395561.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-24/kerala-governors-vegetarian-kitchen-directive-sparks-politic" data-title="Kerala Governor's vegetarian kitchen directive sparks political controversy"><b>Share:</b>
