       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Business Standard · 2026-10-24 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Kotak Mahindra Bank Reports 26% Q2 Profit Increase</h1>
       
       <p>Kotak Mahindra Bank announced a 26% rise in its consolidated net profit for the second quarter, reaching ₹5,645 crore. This growth was reported by Business Standard.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/kotak-mahindra-bank-reports-26-q2-profit-increase.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The bank's standalone profit saw a 29% increase. This was driven by a 16% growth in Net Interest Income (NII) and a reduction in provisions during the quarter.</p><p>However, the bank's net interest margin (NIM) declined to 4.31 per cent. This reduction was attributed to significant FCNR(B) inflows, as per the summary.</p><p>What to watch: Future impact of FCNR(B) inflows on NIM.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate, concise reporting that correctly attributes all key figures and context from the provided summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
