     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-10-24 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Kriti Sanon calls for audience support to bridge industry pay gap</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Actress Kriti Sanon, who is headlining an upcoming large-scale horror film with Maddock Films, recently addressed gender-based pay disparity in the entertainment industry. While acknowledging that more meaty, female-driven roles are being written, she noted that financial remuneration remains tied to box-office returns and theatrical performance.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/kriti-sanon-calls-for-audience-support-to-bridge-industry-pa.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Sanon urged audiences to support women-led projects with the same enthusiasm as male-led films. She emphasized that achieving comparable commercial success is essential to shifting industry calculations regarding budgets and actor fees. By prioritizing content over gender, audiences can play a critical role in incentivizing producers to invest in more female-led theatrical ventures.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief concisely reports Kriti Sanon's perspective on pay parity and the role of audience box-office support, accurately reflecting the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/kriti-sanon-opens-up-on-her-next-solo-lead-with-maddock-films-im-doing-a-film-that-is-on-my-shoulders/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
