       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-24 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Kumaraswamy accuses Karnataka government of shielding suspects</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Union Minister H.D. Kumaraswamy has accused the Karnataka government of protecting key suspects in a sting operation case and irregularities within the Karnataka Public Service Commission (KPSC). He alleged that Home Minister Priyank Kharge is manipulating investigations to target JD(S) workers while shielding the primary individuals involved in the 2023 sting.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/kumaraswamy-accuses-karnataka-government-of-shielding-suspec.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Kumaraswamy further criticized the government’s approach to the KPSC exam scandal, claiming officials moved to the Supreme Court to ensure biased investigators lead the probe. He asserted that the administration is using these investigations as a pretext to blackmail political opponents rather than pursuing a fair resolution.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The summary captures the core accusations made by Kumaraswamy regarding the sting operation and KPSC probe.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/karnataka/state-government-trying-to-protect-accused-in-sting-operation-and-kpsc-cases-says-hdk/article71619869.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
