     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-24 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Maratha activist Manoj Jarange demands probe into audio clip controversy</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Maratha quota activist Manoj Jarange has called on Maharashtra Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis and Deputy Chief Minister Eknath Shinde to launch an investigation into an audio clip controversy. Jarange alleges the clip, which purportedly claims Rs 500 crore was funneled to him through Shiv Sena MP Shrikant Shinde, is part of a broader conspiracy by government-aligned factions to defame him and the quota movement.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/maratha-activist-manoj-jarange-demands-probe-into-audio-clip.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Jarange warned that he will wait 15 to 30 days for a government response before deciding on further action. He insists the administration must hold those responsible accountable, stating that failure to investigate will signal that the community cannot expect justice from the state.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the activist's demands and the context of the audio clip controversy.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/manoj-jarange-audio-clip-row-maharashtra-government-probe-ptag-3024210-2026-10-24?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
