     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-24 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>PM Modi to Unveil Key Projects in Varanasi, Bhubaneswar on October 25</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#National News</span></div>
       <p>Prime Minister Narendra Modi is scheduled to visit Uttar Pradesh and Odisha on Sunday, October 25, 2026, to inaugurate significant projects and witness the Air Force Day aerial display. The visit will include engagements in Varanasi and Bhubaneswar, underscoring the government's focus on infrastructure development, technological advancement, and regional industrial growth across the nation.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/pm-modi-to-unveil-key-projects-in-varanasi-bhubaneswar-on-oc.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In Varanasi, the Prime Minister will attend the Air Force Day Aerial Display-2026 at Namo Ghat, commemorating the 94th anniversary of the Indian Air Force. The aerial show, themed &quot;Wings over Ganges,&quot; will feature a diverse range of aircraft, including the Tejas, Light Combat Helicopter (LCH) Prachand, SU-30MKI, and Rafale, alongside various transport aircraft. This display will also showcase joint operations, with participation from the Indian Navy and the Indian Army, alongside the IAF's premier display teams such as the Surya Kiran Aerobatic Team and the Sarang Helicopter Display Team. Beyond the aerial spectacle, Varanasi will also see the inauguration of Arvind Limited's new garment manufacturing facility. An official statement highlighted this as a crucial step towards strengthening India's textile and apparel manufacturing ecosystem and fostering industrial growth in the region. The facility aims to generate meaningful employment, particularly for women, thereby contributing to the area's economic progress and positioning Uttar Pradesh as a key destination for industrial investment and manufacturing-led growth. The statement also noted that with a global customer base, products manufactured here will reach worldwide, symbolizing women-led development.</p><p>The Prime Minister's itinerary in Bhubaneswar includes the inauguration of the Reserve Bank of India's newly established Data Centre and Cybersecurity Training Institute. This initiative marks a significant milestone in fortifying the technological foundations of India's financial system. The new Data Centre has been meticulously designed to meet the bank's extensive computing requirements, providing a secure, resilient, scalable, and future-ready computing ecosystem for both the RBI and the broader financial sector. It will house four state-of-art data centres, critical for hosting mission-critical payment and settlement systems, along with other flagship initiatives. Notably, this facility has achieved certification to the Uptime Institute Tier IV standard, which is recognized globally as the benchmark for data centre infrastructure, making it one of the largest Tier IV certified facilities within the banking, financial services, and insurance sector worldwide. Concurrently, the Cybersecurity Training Institute is designed to enhance capability building, offering a dedicated institutional platform for comprehensive cybersecurity and enterprise-technology training, research, and sector-wide capability development to safeguard India's digital financial landscape.</p><p>This visit follows earlier significant developments, including the Prime Minister's inauguration of the 594-km Ganga Expressway in Uttar Pradesh, a project praised for contributing to the state's rapid progression towards becoming a one-trillion-dollar economy. Furthermore, a substantial ₹47,000 crore push was previously announced for Odisha, signaling strong tribal outreach and laying the foundation for projects like a ₹25,016 crore coal gasification unit and ₹700 crore of rail infrastructure, with the Prime Minister stating that eastern India is becoming a gateway to progress.</p><p>What to watch: Continued progress on these inaugurated projects and their impact on regional economies.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is comprehensive, well-structured, and accurately synthesizes all key information from the source material regarding the Prime Minister's visit.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/pm-modi-to-visit-varanasi-and-bhubaneswar-on-october-25-inaugurate-key-projects/article71619745.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/bhubaneswar/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bhubaneswar</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
