       <h1>Samiti threatens hunger strike over Yadgir power shortages</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Karnataka Rajya Shoshitara Seva Samiti has announced an indefinite hunger strike in Yadgir starting October 26. The organization is demanding that the Gulbarga Electricity Supply Company (Gescom) provide seven hours of uninterrupted daily power for agricultural pump sets.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/samiti-threatens-hunger-strike-over-yadgir-power-shortages.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>State president Moulali Anapur stated that farmers face severe hardship due to deficient rainfall and erratic power supply, which currently averages six hours daily. The lack of electricity has hindered the irrigation of essential paddy and groundnut crops, leaving farmers concerned about potential harvest losses despite repeated appeals to Gescom officials for improved service.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise, accurate, and includes all essential details from the source text without unnecessary padding.</p>
