       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENVIRONMENT</span> · Guardian Environment · 2026-10-24 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Storm Boelo brings high winds and heavy rain to northern UK</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#environment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The UK faces a second named storm this weekend as Storm Boelo arrives following Storm Austen. Met Office amber alerts cover Scotland, northern England, and Northern Ireland, warning of 80mph gusts and potential danger to life from flying debris. Heavy rain is also expected across Wales and southern England.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/storm-boelo-brings-high-winds-and-heavy-rain-to-northern-uk.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Travel disruptions are anticipated for ferries and trains, with operators advising against non-essential journeys. Thousands remain without power in south-west England from the previous storm, and officials warn similar outages could occur in the north. The Met Office advises residents to stay indoors while the severe weather persists through Sunday.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the storm warnings and current power outage situation using the provided data.</p>
