     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-24 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>TDP-led alliance demands SIT probe into election violence</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A delegation of the TDP-led ruling alliance met State Election Commissioner Anil Chandra Punetha in Vijayawada to demand a Special Investigation Team (SIT) probe into recent violence. The coalition alleges YSRCP activists are orchestrating a criminal conspiracy to disrupt local body elections through attacks on police and the mobilization of anti-social elements from neighboring states.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-24/tdp-led-alliance-demands-sit-probe-into-election-violence.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Alliance leaders rejected Y.S. Jagan Mohan Reddy’s claims of candidate suppression, citing internal party contradictions and widespread legal petitions as evidence of obstruction. They accused the YSRCP of using professional gangsters and rowdy elements to create public panic and undermine the electoral process.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the allegations and the delegation's demands. It is accurate to the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/civil-polls-tdp-led-alliance-seeks-sit-probe-into-alleged-ysrcp-violence/article71620154.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
